      "message": "One thought I had regarding avoiding rebinding if we encounter an already uploaded sort key is that when we write the data to the GPU buffer we check to see if any other data has been written to that the mapped buffer for the same pipeline. If so, then keep that first data as index \u00270\u0027 and calculate the newly written data relative to that. Even if the values between the first uploaded data and the current data were for different pipelines, we\u0027ll have aligned the current data so it\u0027s a multiple of the pipeline\u0027s size so we should get a valid index \u0027x\u0027. Indices that overlap with other pipeline\u0027s data will never be used.\n\nSo this would mean that in the above example with [dataA, dataC, dataB] being the contents of the GPU buffer, the final draw would be \n\n   bind [dataA, ...(junk)..., dataB]\n   bind pipeline1\n   draw with ssbo index \u003d [2, 0]\n   \nWe would still need to rebind if we were forced to move to a new GPU buffer, but that\u0027s unavoidable unless we request the total size needed for each pipeline and upload each pipeline\u0027s list of data in one go.",
